    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "`empirical_cdf()` documents the proportion of observations `<= v`, but currently counts only observations `< v`. For `[1, 2, 2, 3]`, querying `2` returns `0.25` instead of `0.75`; querying the sample maximum also fails to return `1`.\n\nInclude equal observations and add regressions for ties, a constant sample, unsorted input and thresholds outside the sample range. A separate check covers 630 queries against the bundled BEAST/MrBayes posterior samples using sorted ranks as the reference. The Python suites pass on 3.12 and 3.8 with optional PAUP interoperability disabled, and the configured linter passes.\n",
  "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:30:24Z",
